A CONST_DOUBLE's words copied into and out of its fields one HOST_WIDE_INT a field, where GCC 2.8.1 copied them as
one block. The block holds only where an rtx's field is as wide as a HOST_WIDE_INT; on a host whose pointers are wider
than int (LP64) a field is wider, and every floating-point constant cc1 compiles loses its high word.

